# Prepared Flow normal-host browser review

**Prepared only; no host or browser has started.** Root owns actual CUA/browser actions and any acceptance claims. The fixture never touches user4311.

After authenticating preparation-validation.json and preparation-manifest.json, root may launch `node work/root-flow-link-browser-review-next/host.mjs --run`. It prints only the ephemeral normal Studio URL/PID and nonsensitive seed name. The private close URL/token are written solely to ignored `.local/private-control.json`; never publish or print those values. The normal shared host retains its own exact session, origin, token and static-route behavior. No bridge or handler substitution is used.

Navigate the owned URL ending `/#flow`. In **Saved native flows**, select **Owned static Link In/Out fixture**. Its outgoing links array is empty while the incoming list references Out, so the server union draws a dashed Out→In connection. The physical Out→physical-debug wire is retained in raw JSON but overridden. Use Disconnect static link and verify both lists remove the pair and the dashed edge disappears; Connect static link should restore both lists and the dashed edge. Save draft, Deploy, then inject an owned synthetic message. The Debug result should use virtual-debug only and include `_event: "node:out"`. Metadata/physical wires should survive these edits; durable history/context are checked after shutdown by reopening the owned disk store without another host start.

Use an authenticated POST to the private close URL with the `X-Owned-Control` token read locally from the ignored control file. The collector also closes on its fifteen-minute deadline or SIGINT/SIGTERM. It reads final export/inspection/validation, closes the normal host/control, authenticates all457 candidate records and13 source copies again, then removes only its own prefixed temporary data and private control file. If cleanup/final reads fail, raw errors are retained; a host receipt alone never claims browser acceptance.

Wire evidence contains only time, phase, method, path and status; no query/body/header/token logging. Seed and final-read requests are labeled separately. Native archive/executable/oracle packages are not copied. The original Node-RED executable/runtime is not started by this fixture. The collector is newly written, guided by the existing Vault host's lifecycle pattern; no Vault diagnostic or acceptance facts are transferred to Flow.
